      },
      "text": "Modernism in architecture is a program, not just a style. The program: reject all\nhistorical ornament, embrace industrial production methods, design rationally for\nfunction, and produce a universal architecture for the modern age. The structural\ninnovation that enables it (reinforced concrete + steel skeleton) was already in place\nfrom the Chicago School. Modernism is a philosophical decision about what to do with\nthat structural freedom."
    },
